  ✔ keeps a parked 0 kt aircraft At gate (0.177296ms)
  ✔ shows first 2–5 kt movement as Pushback (0.07332ms)
  ✔ shows sustained 8–20 kt movement as Taxiing out (0.050745ms)
  ✔ does not return to At gate through a stale surface gap (0.052787ms)
  ✔ keeps Taxiing out monotonic once its latch is established (0.134267ms)
  ✔ preserves the existing takeoff transition (0.092872ms)
  ✔ renders Pushback and Taxiing out as separate passenger stages (0.763451ms)
✔ first-class pushback and taxi-out stages (1.538852ms)
▶ on the move evidence
  ✔ UA219: keeps an overdue estimate non-actual, then records only observed/provider push (91.39939ms)
  ✔ UA219: reconstructs the first stand exit from track history instead of the 10:03 taxi classification (0.44113ms)
  ✔ UA219: replaces a persisted detected time copied from the 9:25 estimate (0.098194ms)
  ✔ preserves a genuine earlier movement latch when it did not copy an estimate (0.0661ms)
  ✔ labels the passenger operational event Pushback, not Departure (0.707057ms)
  ✔ UA3600: never regresses from Taxiing out to Pushback during normal surface changes (155.126557ms)
  ✔ does not advance a stationary aircraft just because scheduled departure passed (20.696983ms)
✔ on the move evidence (268.983993ms)
✔ preserves missing weather feeds as unknown while the flight still loads (22.802188ms)
